  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q5_PatchPanel
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: A patch panel port is terminated to T568A. What must the wall outlet
    at the other end of that run use?
  choices:
  - T568B, so the pairs cross over
  - Either one; the switch corrects it automatically
  - "T568A \u2014 both ends of a horizontal run use the same standard"
  - Whichever the colour code on the outlet shows first
  correctChoiceIndex: 2
  points: 10
  explanation: A horizontal run is a straight-through link. Mixing standards at the
    two ends turns the permanent link into a cross-over, which is why an installation
    picks one standard and uses it everywhere.
